 (r"We build a HANFIS with a reduced rule base and intermediate variables designed to be interpretable, test how faithful its rule-level explanations are (Section~\ref{sec:e6}), and ask whether it preserves or improves estimation error relative to a flat ANFIS and, more demandingly, relative to two baselines that need no neuro-fuzzy training: a 4-week persistence forecast and a formula of two inputs. On the realised exploitability-exposure target the answer is mostly negative. The label is dominated by its own recent history, HANFIS is not distinguishable from persistence, and a four-parameter formula beats it in a pre-registered forward window. The paper reports that result together with the frozen protocol, the post hoc analyses that explain it, and the limits of what the data can show. Policy support and edge execution are designed but left to future work.",
  r"We build a HANFIS with a reduced rule base and intermediate variables meant to be interpretable, test how faithful its rule-level explanations are (Section~\ref{sec:e6}), and compare its estimation error with flat ANFIS variants and with two baselines that need no neuro-fuzzy training: a 4-week persistence forecast and a formula of two inputs. On the realised exploitability-exposure target the answer is mostly negative. The label is dominated by its own recent history, HANFIS is not distinguishable from persistence, and a four-parameter formula beats it in a pre-registered forward window. The paper reports that result with the frozen protocol, the post hoc analyses that explain it, and the limits of what the data can show."),
